                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b102a8ae-9c5c-4c94-be17-b5228cd7415d",
                        "entry_id": "a0a2a1c0-da3a-3b53-a188-b20866706914",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ozones"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2215439a-3f46-3779-a165-e02057ff4e1a",
                        "entry_id": "a0a2a1c0-da3a-3b53-a188-b20866706914",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An allotrope of oxygen (symbol O₃) having three atoms in the molecule instead of the usual two; it is a toxic gas, generated from oxygen by electrical discharge."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "99a5f299-2d3a-4aa3-9766-f910fe7c5f94",
                                "sense_id": "2215439a-3f46-3779-a165-e02057ff4e1a",
                                "text": "Lightning flashed again, the thunder came a second later. It rained harder. The smell of ozone was strong. You could feel the charge in the air."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "316a6449-4f3a-3c45-a79b-7c511f0625cd",
                        "entry_id": "a0a2a1c0-da3a-3b53-a188-b20866706914",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fresh air, especially that breathed at the seaside and smelling of seaweed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British",
                            "informal",
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "920cfe3b-94fa-4026-8f6a-1390e545b362",
                                "sense_id": "316a6449-4f3a-3c45-a79b-7c511f0625cd",
                                "text": "A patent obtained in England, and specified far from clearly, for obtaining ozone by boiling seaweed,†† may be mentioned as a curiosity, and also the credulity with which ozone-baths, prepared in this manner, find a ready sale, in spite of, or perhaps rather on account of, their high price."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3622afa1-061d-49a7-8dde-dad898207cf9",
                                "sense_id": "316a6449-4f3a-3c45-a79b-7c511f0625cd",
                                "text": "To Ramsgate baths she sped, in quest / Of seaweed and ozone ; / For seaweed and ozone were best, / They said, to give her tone."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56a4eac3-6d6f-4fd7-b39f-8f6a96623336",
                                "sense_id": "316a6449-4f3a-3c45-a79b-7c511f0625cd",
                                "text": "It's got the lot: fresh sea air, ozone, seaweed. You could cut the air with a knife."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
